# 01 — BaseQueuedWriter: centralized queue + backpressure base class

## Goal

Extract queue management, backpressure, and worker-dispatch logic out of
`MLDPWriter` into a reusable `BaseQueuedWriter<Item>` abstract class so every
writer that needs internal queuing inherits it for free.

---

## Motivation

`MLDPWriter` owns three concerns that are writer-agnostic:

1. **Bounded MPSC queue** — `channels_[]`, `queuedItems_`, `WorkerChannel`
2. **Backpressure** — `backpressureMutex_`, `backpressureCv_`, blocking push
3. **Worker thread pool** — `threadPool_`, `workerLoop(i)` dispatch

`HDF5WriterBase` independently re-implements a similar bounded queue + thread
pair.  Unifying both under one base eliminates drift and gives future writers a
consistent contract.

---

## New class: `BaseQueuedWriter<Item>`

**Location**: `include/writer/BaseQueuedWriter.h` + `src/writer/BaseQueuedWriter.cpp`
(or header-only if template; prefer header-only template with explicit instantiation
guards to keep compile times sane).

### Template parameter
- `Item` — the per-worker queue element type.  Each concrete subclass defines its
  own `Item` (e.g. `MLDPWriter::QueueItem`, `HDF5WriterBase::WriteBatch`).

### Public API (mirrors `IWriter`, inherits from it)

```cpp
// Lifecycle — final; subclass hooks called internally
void start() final;    // calls doStart() after thread pool is up
void stop() noexcept final;    // drains queues, calls doStop()
void forceStop() noexcept final;

// Default push: filters payload, serializes to Item via toItem(),
// then applies backpressure + enqueues.
// Subclass may override entirely if needed.
bool push(util::bus::IDataBus::EventBatch batch) noexcept override;
```

### Protected pure virtuals (subclass contract)

```cpp
// Convert an accepted EventBatch into zero or more queue Items.
// Return empty vector to silently drop.
virtual std::vector<Item> toItems(util::bus::IDataBus::EventBatch& batch) = 0;

// Process one dequeued Item.  Called from a worker thread.
virtual void processItem(std::size_t workerIndex, Item item) = 0;

// Optional lifecycle hooks
virtual void doStart() {}   // called after threads are up
virtual void doStop()  {}   // called after all threads join
```

### Protected non-virtual helpers (provided by base)

```cpp
// Notify backpressure CV (call from processItem after consuming work)
void notifySlotFree();

// Current queue depth across all channels
std::size_t queueDepth() const noexcept;

// Config accessors
int  workerCount() const noexcept;
int  queueCapacity() const noexcept;
```

### Backpressure contract

- `push()` blocks per-item when `queuedItems_ >= queueCapacity`.
- Unblocks on: slot freed (`notifySlotFree()`), `running_` → false, or
  `forceQuit_` → true.
- `push_timeout_ms` from config: if > 0, blocking push times out and returns
  `false` instead of blocking forever.  Currently `MLDPWriter` blocks
  indefinitely — fix this in migration.

### Config fields (base reads from `IWriterConfig` or passed struct)

```
queue_capacity     int   default 200
worker_count       int   default 8    (replaces threadPoolSize)
push_timeout_ms    int   default 0    (0 = block forever)
```

